    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0531" n="435" xml:id="pg435"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Baron de Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 538.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In accordance with your request I
                    transmitted at once a copy of your latest notes on the subject of the Italian
                    bureau to my colleague of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>I regret once more to have to inform your excellency that this Government does
                    not see its way clear to reopen the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
